\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces FedRAS system architecture and round pipeline. The edge aggregator \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {estimates client link states, }}\DIFdelendFL  scores every client--rank pair with the delivery hazard \eqref  {eq:hazard} and the saturating capacity \eqref  {eq:cap}, and computes the client--rank assignment with the \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {exact }}\DIFdelendFL  grid-based dynamic program under the byte budget and the admission cap\DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {(Proposition~\ref {prop:dp}). Admitted clients train on a frozen backbone with LoRA factors sliced to the assigned rank and upload only the trainable factor $B$, at 5.63\,KB per rank column; the shared factor $A$ is never transmitted}}\DIFdelendFL  . Updates arriving within the deadline $\tau $ pass the on-time gate and are aggregated \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {rank-maskedly }}\DIFdelendFL  \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue}\uwave {with rank-masked averaging }}\DIFaddendFL  while \DIFaddbeginFL  {\color {blue}\uwave {the shared factor }}\DIFaddendFL  $A$ stays frozen\DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {(Proposition~\ref {prop:agg})}}\DIFdelendFL  ; \DIFdelbeginFL  {\color {red}\sout {late or lost updates are discarded, and the }}\DIFdelendFL  observed outcomes update the link-state history.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{7}{}{}{}}
